E AX3060 640-region-escape-store.ax:48:12-13 region-escape "parameter `x`, which lives in region `@s`, is stored into the field `s` of a value, which lives in region `@r`" ?"MM-RGN-3 (docs/memory-model-v2-design.md): a value may be stored only into a place its own region OUTLIVES, because the place is still readable after the value's region has been reclaimed. A region named in a signature (`@r`) outlives the function's own region and is unordered against another name; the function's own region is its caller's. Keep the value in the region of the place it is stored into - allocate it there, or copy it there - or widen the place's annotation to the value's region"
